update public.local_businesses set description = $q$In the heart of Shetland&rsquo;s capital of Lerwick, the Grand Hotel offers comfortable ensuite rooms, free parking and excellent service to guests year-round. With local shops, restaurants and bars on your doorstep, the Grand Hotel gives you a base like no other to take in all Lerwick and Shetland has to offer.$q$ where id = '889c1c1b-94ee-4110-b816-8ad8b2194e5a';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Shetland Fish Ltd is at the forefront of an exciting time for the Shetland fishing industry. Shetland&rsquo;s fishing industry is undergoing a renaissance. The fleet is modernising to take advantage of the healthy, sustainable fish stocks which gather around Shetland&rsquo;s wild coast. Four of our main stocks haddock, coley, hake and plaice still hold MSC status and our onshore infrastructure is improving with two new fish markets currently being built. The Shetland Islands is located in the midst of some of the most prolific fishing grounds in Europe. Shetland is the second largest whitefish landing port in the UK. Our buying team is dedicated to helping our customers access some of the finest, freshest whitefish available. We are passionate about the high quality of seafood landed in Shetland, and we are proud to play our part in connecting buyers from all over the UK and Europe with this outstanding source of fresh fish. If you would like to become a valued partner in Shetland fish, please contact us.$q$ where id = '150e7903-395a-42ae-87da-39a81d266d64';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Who we are We are Scotland&rsquo;s award-winning national tourism organisation. As a publicly-funded body (an NDPB, or &lsquo;non-departmental government body&rsquo;) we are accountable to the Minister for Enterprise, Energy and Tourism. Why we&rsquo;re here - the facts Our main aim to contribute significantly to the advancement of Scottish tourism by giving it a real presence in the global marketplace and benefiting the whole of Scotland. A strong and vibrant tourism sector is crucial for a successful economy. Currently tourism contributes &pound;11.6 billion to the Scottish economy each year (direct and indirect impact), as well as supporting over 180,000 jobs. In Shetland these figures are approximately &pound;16.5 million & 1200 jobs. As well as being a major employer in Scotland, the sector underpins the success of others such as transport, retail, farming, food and drink and construction.* * Deloitte study, 2013 Where we are Our local activities are organised around six regions and three island areas. In Shetland we have the Visitor Information Centres in Market Cross, Lerwick, & at Sumburgh Airport, plus the VisitScotland office above Market Cross. What we do Our purpose is to grow and develop the sustainable economic benefit of tourism to Scotland's economy. This purpose is supported by five Corporate Objectives, which are closely linked: 1. Marketing: We will market Scotland and its outstanding assets to visitors from all parts of the world. This including the promotion of Scotland to people living in Scotland - encouraging them to visit different parts of the country 2. Information provision: We will provide information and inspiration to visitors both locally and globally via their preferred choice of medium (online, print, face-to-face) 3. Quality and sustainability: we will provide support and advice to businesses, with the goal of improving the quality and sustainability of the tourism sector in Scotland. We will provide assurance to visitors through our quality schemes. 4. Working in partnership: We will listen to and work with the industry, partners and stakeholders to shape our offering and support. 5. Events: We will maximise the benefits from the 'Winning Years' and their legacy. We will implement the national events strategy, and sustain, develop and promote Scotland's international profile as one of the world's foremost events destinations.$q$ where id = '003d8ae8-21cb-4253-a503-1c3e5cd879d3';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$The oldest bar in Shetland, a very popular public house situated on Lerwick&rsquo;s harbour front &ndash; keeping customers refreshed since 1895! A warm, welcoming bar serving very wide range of wines, beers and spirits including fine malts (ask for the menu) as well as freshly ground coffee. The bar has had a few name changes since a public house was first opened on the site. We understand it was first named the Seaview Vaults before the harbour, as we know it now, was built. It then became the Thule Refreshment Bar, around the 1895 mark. We know the bar lost its drinks license in 1920 when a Veto Poll in Lerwick returned a result that saw the town of Lerwick become &ldquo;dry&rdquo;. Just what were the folk thinking? We think they just sold peanuts and crisps for a few years during that great catastrophe! Lerwick became a &ldquo;wet&rdquo; town again in 1947 and The Thule Bar began to pour beer once more, we&rsquo;ve been keeping the good citizens of Shetland and our many welcome visitors refreshed ever since. Cheers!$q$ where id = 'e5178378-a61f-4a01-bc9a-6979ac5f8fac';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$JLP Internet- Shetland Web Design and Online Services. Here at JLP Internet we help businesses unlock the power of the Internet to reach more customers online and become more efficient. We are proud to work with businesses in Shetland and throughout the UK, offering cost effective web design services to businesses of all sizes - from self employed to multi million pound international companies. Having a website is only one part of a successful online strategy. That&rsquo;s why as well as a full website creation service, we also offer custom software solutions built to fit your needs, managed office 365 to streamline your office and internet marketing and search engine optimisation to promote yourself more effectively online.$q$ where id = 'ca08ead8-339a-4a27-a183-8d1e162387b4';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$We are a small family-owned business committed to using and showcasing the very best of Shetland produce. Since launching Island Larder in 2017 we have revamped and grown the business several times, including overhauling our operation during the Covid-19 pandemic, launching a host of new products including artisan ice-cream and an expanded range of fudge and other confectionary items. We are so passionate about all things Shetland and have always wanted to run an independent business taking advantage of all the fantastic local ingredients that are available right on our doorstep. Island Larder is proud to be marketing and showcasing both of these beloved facets of Shetland culture to the wider world because we simply just love our home islands and want to spread the word about this special place as far and wide as we can. Shetland&rsquo;s capital Lerwick is the home of our premises, in the heart of Lerwick&rsquo;s historic and picturesque town centre, where we produce all of our confectionary items. The building itself, on Commercial Street, is steeped in history and was formerly run as Smiths of Lerwick, a family-run clothing shop for many decades. Both my granny and my husband&rsquo;s granny worked in the store, and we use the same bunker that they served from today, made by hand with all the original dents, scrapes and stories.$q$ where id = '0db30912-071e-41bb-a34a-03619ec7a5d9';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$On Lerwick&rsquo;s seafront, the former lodberries, turned hotel, offers comfortable rooms to visitors to Shetland in the heart of &lsquo;old&rsquo; Lerwick. With a view across Lerwick&rsquo;s harbour to Bressay, Queens Hotel offers guests the perfect location for those that want to take in all that Lerwick has to offer. The Hotel is a stones throw from the pier which makes Queens a great shore base for visiting crews. The hotel caters for all types of guests, those needing a town base for a couple of days through to those who are visiting longer term, whether that&rsquo;s due to work or longer family visits. The accommodation at Queens offers well appointed, quality accommodation to suit all. The accommodation comprises: 8 Single Bedrooms 6 Double Bedrooms 12 Twin Bedrooms 1 Triple Bedroom Each room includes: Ensuite Television WiFi Appropriate Working Space The Queens Hotel is currently underdoing refurbishment and we do not currently offer breakfast or restaurant/bar facilities. However, there are many shops, cafes, restaurants and bars along the street and we would be more than happy to make recommendations to make your stay in Shetland the best it can be!$q$ where id = '9505776a-7f4b-4375-b067-0f003e2320fc';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$In 1986 Ken Beer began writing cost control software for BP Sullom Voe. The oil terminal was one of Europe&rsquo;s largest, based in Shetland, a remote island half way between Scotland and Norway. The software was so successful that BP deployed it on multi-million dollar projects across the globe. Their cost of ownership dropped because it ran on IBM PCs, rather than the common mainframes of the day. In 1992, Ken met three friends near Kildrummy Castle in the Scottish Highlands, to found a company that would take cutting edge cost control solutions to some of the world&rsquo;s largest oil and gas projects. That night, Kildrummy&reg; was born. We soon opened offices in Houston, Texas, to service all the oil majors, independents and JVs who were rolling out Kildrummy&reg; software. Twenty-six years later, Kildrummy is still building flexible systems that fit our customers&rsquo; policies and practices, because we believe in exceptional projects and exceptional service. That&rsquo;s why our customers trust our software to manage trillions of dollars in project cost world-wide.$q$ where id = '5792dc67-a181-4090-9d5f-30428f3cbb52';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$NGR Accountancy was founded with a clear goal&mdash;to remove the stress and complexity of accounting for small businesses and self-employed professionals. After more than a decade working in a traditional accountancy practice, founder Neil recognized that many small businesses weren&rsquo;t getting the hands-on support they needed. With this in mind, NGR Accountancy was established to provide a client-focused approach, ensuring business owners can leave the numbers in expert hands and concentrate on running their businesses. The firm is built around a simple question: What do small business owners really need from their accountant? NGR Accountancy takes care of the financial details, so clients can focus on what matters most.$q$ where id = 'e03193e6-5e86-422e-a479-d09b5f2af136';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$High Level Music has been in business for 21 years. They moved into their new shop 5 years ago and the business has gone from strength to strength. You can find lots on offer at High Level Music such as: &bull; Instruments for sale &bull; Instrument repair &bull; Music equipment &bull; Music school If you are visiting Shetland on holiday and haven&rsquo;t brought your instrument with you then don&rsquo;t despair, you can hire a guitar/fiddle or ukulele from High Level Music. If you would like to teach music, then please contact Fiona on 01595 692618 to ask about renting a space at the shop to teach. If learning how to play an instrument is something you are interested in then please contact High Level Music to arrange. Fiona and her team are very knowledgeable about instruments and equipment, if you have seen something you would like to know more about, they may be able to get it into the shop for you.$q$ where id = '3b3d76fd-ec58-4b46-a5f1-89cb717796cc';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Established in 1947, George Robertson (Shetland) Ltd has been in business for more than 75 years and is proud to be Shetland&rsquo;s leading electrical contractor (GR Contracting), electrical appliance retailer (GR Direct), and kitchen design studio (GR Kitchens). GR Contracting - We provide electrical services within retail, domestic, commercial and industrial sectors, taking great pride in our ability to deliver on projects, no matter how large or small by always ensuring we provide a first-class service from initial contact to the completion and beyond for each project. GR Direct &ndash; We offer a wide range of home electricals at competitive prices; from televisions to fridge freezers, and washing machines to home sound systems. We are trusted dealers of well-known brands such as Bosch, Neff, Siemens, Sony, Sonos, Blomberg, Beko, Dyson, Shark, Rangemaster, Ninja and many more. We have built a reputation for great customer service, competitive pricing, and expertise in sales and aftercare. GR Kitchens &ndash; We provide world-renowned, high-quality kitchens to suit a range of budgets. Our experienced designers can ease you through the whole process - design, supply and installation. Visit our website to find out more about the services and products we offer: www.grdirect.co.uk$q$ where id = 'a88e5fbd-1806-49e3-9087-70389356bdfe';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Radiance Shetland &ndash; Your One-Stop Beauty Destination Originally starting as a tanning salon, Radiance Shetland has grown into a full-service beauty hub offering expert hair, nail, and beauty treatments. We are thrilled to be the first in Shetland to introduce permanent jewelry &ndash; a unique and stylish way to symbolize lasting bonds between friends, family, or couples. From sunbed sessions to cutting-edge hair styling and manicures, Radiance is your go-to destination for all things beauty. We look forward to welcoming you and helping you look and feel your best! Services include professional hair dressing, sunbed sessions for that perfect glow, and beauty treatments tailored to your needs. Radiance Shetland also offers the latest trend in permanent jewellery, where you can get custom-fitted bracelets and anklets that last. Visit Radiance Shetland for a full pampering experience, combining beauty, style, and luxury all in one place.$q$ where id = '8ffde8a0-198e-4bd3-878c-be720cd3e30e';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Envi is a family-run hair salon located centrally at 110 Commercial Street, Lerwick. Conveniently situated near bus routes and with ample nearby parking, Envi is easily accessible for all clients. A skilled and talented team of hairdressers is dedicated to delivering top-quality hair services. Bookable appointments and walk-ins are both available to accommodate various schedules. The salon uses a range of high-quality products, including Matrix, Colour Evo, and L&rsquo;Or&eacute;al. Additionally, clients can purchase products to maintain their hair care routine at home. Catering to all clients with a range of services, including cutting, colouring, styling, blow-drying, and barber services. Additional Treatments: Offering nails, makeup, bridal and occasion hair, and more. For any requests or queries, feel free to send a message, and the team will be delighted to assist. Visit Envi for a personalised and professional hair care experience.$q$ where id = '26b88f3d-04b1-4a95-a128-a140da0bd1f4';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Here at the Shetland Soap Company, our soap and skincare range is inspired by the islands' raw elements, and are hand crafted using both traditional and contemporary methods to combine the very best natural ingredients. Added to that, all our products are handmade by people who really care about what they do. People with learning disabilities that are extremely proud of the work they do. Incredible products from incredible people. Shetland Soap Company is proudly part of COPE Ltd, one of Scotland&rsquo;s leading social enterprises, providing employment and employment skill development for adults with disabilities. Find out more about COPE Ltd at www.cope.ltd.co.uk To see our range of products or to buy online visit www.shetlandsoap.co.uk$q$ where id = '7511b3df-4cc6-479b-b62e-04715a22cd7c';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$R. Robertson & Son Ltd are Shetland&rsquo;s largest transport operator, based in the main town of Lerwick. Providing private hires and tours within Shetland and the UK Mainland, for both national and international travel agencies, as well as local customers. Small groups from two people to hundreds of people can be catered for, along with bespoke tours and itineraries. Operations include private hire taxis, public service and home to school transport. The Lerwick workshop does contract maintenance for fleet customers as well as in house maintenance.$q$ where id = '046e0707-3985-48da-9506-f4a4f6c071af';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Conochie's Newsagents, the most popular newsagent in Shetland, is conveniently located in the heart of Lerwick's town centre. Known for its wide range of products and services, Conochie's is a one-stop shop for locals and visitors alike. News and Magazines: A comprehensive selection of newspapers and magazines covering various interests and topics. Thornton&rsquo;s Chocolates: An exclusive Thornton&rsquo;s chocolate franchise offering a delightful array of premium chocolates. Cards and Gifts: A great selection of greeting cards for all occasions and unique gifts to suit every taste. Post Office Facilities: Convenient post office services available within the store, making it easy to handle mailing needs.$q$ where id = '2aa72f2f-d4dd-425b-baa8-a9259491ed56';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$The Cancer Research Shop in Lerwick Town Centre stands as a beacon of community spirit and charitable endeavour. Located in Harrison Sq, this shop is dedicated to supporting life-saving cancer research through the sale of high-quality, pre-loved items. What Shoppers Will Find: &bull; Clothing: A diverse selection of men's, women's, and children's apparel, ranging from casual wear to formal attire. &bull; Books: A variety of books across all genres, catering to every type of reader. &bull; Homeware: Unique and stylish items designed to enhance any home d&eacute;cor. &bull; Accessories: A range of jewellery, handbags, shoes, and more to complement any outfit. &bull; Toys and Games: Fun and educational toys for children of all ages. Donations: The shop welcomes donations of gently used clothing, books, homeware, and more. These contributions support the mission and enable continued operations.$q$ where id = '227a3fab-2db6-42ca-b021-aa1b2bd21f0b';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Shetland artist, born in 1975 on the most northerly island in Scotland, the Shetland Islands, draws inspiration from the local landscape. Having grown up in Lerwick, they loved playing in the lanes as a child and now enjoy drawing them. The different textures and shades, especially of the cobblestones, trees, and steps, captivate them. The way the light changes the atmosphere of the lanes is fascinating, and the history of this special part of Lerwick, along with its stories, intrigues them. They strive to capture the stillness and sense of timelessness in their drawings. Bigton, located at the south end of Shetland, was another favorite childhood haunt. It was home to their grandparents, where they spent many happy days playing in the hay and fields with Shetland ponies, cows, sheep, and playful little lambs. Recently, the artist has returned to their &lsquo;Ness&rsquo; roots to celebrate the islands&rsquo; unique landscape. Their latest collections include paintings of abandoned 'yoals' (rowing boats), old croft houses, wildlife, and Shetland&rsquo;s beautiful wildflowers.$q$ where id = '578d5ff6-d185-4a82-a9ae-2ea41b4bf57f';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$The British Red Cross has been helping millions of people in the UK and around the world get the support they need when crisis strikes. From hiring a wheelchair or dealing with loneliness, to adjusting to life in a new country - we&rsquo;re there when you need us. The Red Cross Charity Shop plays a vital role in raising funds for the Red Cross&rsquo;s humanitarian efforts. This shop offers a diverse array of goods, both new and gently used, ensuring there is something for everyone. What Shoppers Will Find: &bull; Clothing: A wide selection of new and pre-loved men&rsquo;s, women&rsquo;s, and children&rsquo;s apparel. &bull; Books: An assortment of books covering various genres and interests. &bull; Homeware: Unique home d&eacute;cor items to add charm and style to any living space. &bull; Accessories: A range of jewellery, handbags, shoes, and other accessories to complete any outfit. &bull; Toys and Games: A variety of toys and games for children of all ages. Reasons to Visit: &bull; Support Humanitarian Efforts: Purchases contribute directly to funding the Red Cross&rsquo;s vital services and aid programs. &bull; Eco-Friendly Shopping: Buying pre-loved items helps reduce waste and promote sustainability. &bull; Community Engagement: The shop serves as a local hub for those who want to support a worthy cause and connect with their community. Donations: The Red Cross Charity Shop gratefully accepts donations of new and gently used items, including clothing, books, homeware, and more. Contributions help support their ongoing humanitarian work.$q$ where id = '49bcf49e-d262-49b8-a4e8-9306449d16c2';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Universal Stores brings together two lovely things in life, beautiful flowers and irresistible sweet treats. Whether you&rsquo;re picking up a fresh bouquet for a special occasion, a thoughtful gift, or just something to brighten your day, you&rsquo;ll find a great selection to choose from. Alongside the florals, you&rsquo;ll also discover a sweetie shop packed with favourites for all ages &ndash; from classic treats to fun goodies that make perfect gifts or a wee indulgence. Pop in for a browse, a chat, and leave with something that&rsquo;ll make you (or someone else) smile.$q$ where id = '9752a26c-2830-4ffa-a5ea-caae1b6d76a4';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$The Shetland Times is Shetland&rsquo;s longest-running weekly newspaper, keeping the community informed with trusted local news, features, sport and opinion for over a century. Published every week, the paper covers stories from across the isles, alongside in-depth reporting on local issues, community events, culture and business. The Shetland Times plays an important role in supporting Shetland&rsquo;s communities by sharing stories that matter and providing a platform for local voices.$q$ where id = '0981d837-6692-45b5-aad3-f970f6306955';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Bringing a taste of home baking into Lerwick town centre, The Original Cake Fridge is the perfect spot for something sweet. Alongside their famous cakes and traybakes, you&rsquo;ll also find tea, coffee, and a lovely range of gifts for all occasions. Whether you&rsquo;re popping in for a treat, a cuppa, or a unique present, The Cake Fridge offers a warm welcome right in the heart of the town.$q$ where id = 'b202febd-16e3-4514-8952-5bd5704bdecc';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Shetland Islands Council has identified improving data communication services across the Isles as one of its key targets. To help meet this aspiration the SIC has set up the Shetland Telecom Project. Its remit is to improve data communications. The Shetland Telecom Project was established in 2009 to undertake a significant step change in telecoms provision in Shetland. The project has successfully achieved the provision of resilient, reliable, high capacity data services for Shetland. The project is part of Shetland Islands Council&rsquo;s Economic Development Unit. The fibre optic network which it now manages was part funded by the EU. The Shetland Telecom Project is a member of the Internet Service Providers Association (ISPA) and the Independent Network Cooperative Association (INCA).$q$ where id = 'e3169e58-bacd-4f96-966c-260572a236a6';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Located in the centre of Lerwick, Shetland Somatic Arts is a modern, welcoming tattoo and piercing studio known for its creativity, professionalism, and attention to detail. This unique self-care studio offers a diverse range of services, bringing together a collective of experienced practitioners to create a welcoming and holistic environment. The space is home to Lymfastr&ouml;m Therapy, offering both manual lymphatic drainage and Swedish massage. Lymphatic massage is particularly beneficial for post-surgical recovery and for individuals undergoing cancer treatments. From next month, The Brow Arc. Co will also be joining the studio, providing a range of brow and beauty treatments. In addition, Jody Does Jels and Education delivers accredited gel nail courses throughout the week. At the heart of the studio is an experienced tattoo artist and body piercer, specialising in the hand-poked, machine-free tattoo method. With piercing experience since 2012 and tattooing since 2013, their work is grounded in both skill and care. Alongside their creative practice, they are currently in their final year of counselling studies at UHI, bringing an added depth of understanding to their approach. This combination of experience allows the studio to offer a truly person-centred, body-led, and trauma-informed service. Each client is treated holistically, with respect for their personal history, nervous system, and individual responses. Rather than rushing procedures, clients are given the time and space they need to feel comfortable, process their experience, and fully engage with the experience. Recognising that tattoos and piercings often hold deep personal meaning, the studio supports clients in marking significant moments in their lives&mdash;whether beginnings, transitions, or endings. Client autonomy and informed consent are central to every aspect of the service, creating a safe, respectful, and empowering environment for all. Please remember that all services are by appointment only, and it&rsquo;s important to bring an acceptable form of photo ID to access our services. Here&rsquo;s what you can bring: &bull; Passport &bull; Driver's License &bull; Provisional License &bull; Young Scot Card For younger clients (under 16 years), they kindly ask that a legal parent is present. You&rsquo;ll also need to bring: &bull; Consent and photo ID from the other legal parent (if they are not attending) &bull; Full Birth Certificate &bull; Young Scot Card &bull; A form of photo ID for the attending legal parent from the list above If you have any questions or need further assistance, please don&rsquo;t hesitate to send them an email or message, and a member of their caring team will respond as soon as possible.$q$ where id = 'b99ae0df-4c9b-42f9-9c23-b6ba7a83b92d';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Shetland Aerogenerators was formed in 1992, and we operate from our offices on Charlotte Street in Shetland&rsquo;s capital of Lerwick. We initially set out to investigate the opportunities expected after the Government announced the Scottish Renewables Obligation. Shetland Aerogenerators owns Burradale Windfarm and we have acted as developer, constructor, operator and client at various stages.$q$ where id = '0d9012b3-5748-4b6b-84b7-1c7bd86a1e5c';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Reset Wellbeing Therapies is founded by Jennie, whose lifelong passion for caring spans nursing, social care, dementia support, oncology massage and over 30 years practising Reiki. With a career rooted in holistic, compassionate support, Jennie brings together clinical experience and spiritual awareness to care for the whole person &mdash; emotionally, physically and socially. Based at The Mission on Harbour Street in Lerwick town centre, Reset Wellbeing Therapies offers a wide range of tailored treatments including deep tissue and pregnancy massage, oncology massage, hot stone and Ayurvedic therapies, Reiki, reflexology, lymphatic drainage and bespoke self-care packages. Each session is personalised, reflecting Jennie&rsquo;s belief that wellbeing is never one-size-fits-all. Room 7, The Mission &ndash; Creativity & Wellness Centre, 2 Harbour Street, Lerwick, ZE1 0LR$q$ where id = 'c25b113a-0e48-4fc4-a05e-6e264be57faf';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Caf&eacute; offering breakfast and lunch in the historic Solotti's & Faerdie Maet premises. Check out Pete's Facebook page for daily specials$q$ where id = 'ed502629-d893-46cc-a74b-5d4ee5115cd4';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$The Peerie Shop 'theonestoppresentshop', in front of the Peerie Shop Caf&eacute; on the Esplanade. A huge range of carefully chosen colourful interesting gifts from around the world. Fair trade, ethically sourced, British, and produced by us. Victoria Gibson hand-knitted designer knitwear and its own range of Shetland t-shirts, postcards, bags, fridge magnets and badges. A good selection of books, bowls, decorations, scarves, jewellery, cards, candles, boxes and glasses.$q$ where id = '796a8ec6-d7a4-4af0-b77b-460ca31ab1da';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Looking for proper, delicious pizza? This local favourite serves up freshly made pizzas packed with flavour, using quality ingredients. Whether you&rsquo;re after a classic Margherita, a meat-loaded feast, or something a little different, there&rsquo;s something for everyone on the menu. Perfect takeaway for a night in! With a warm welcome and a passion for great food, it&rsquo;s no wonder this pizzeria is a go-to spot for both locals and visitors. Pop in and see what&rsquo;s cooking &ndash; you might just find your new favourite pizza place!$q$ where id = '80279ba9-c838-43f5-a10c-fd7ca33e4802';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Located in the heart of Lerwick town centre, Meraki is a modern and welcoming hair salon offering professional hairdressing services. With a focus on creativity, care and attention to detail, the team at Meraki provides everything from precision cuts and colouring to styling for special occasions. Whether you're looking for a fresh new look, a subtle refresh, or expert advice on maintaining healthy hair, you&rsquo;ll find a friendly and relaxed experience in this stylish town centre salon.$q$ where id = 'ca15a252-92a2-4863-9ecf-857b475ad853';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$We are a small family run company based in the Shetland Islands. All of our soaps and bath products are handmade by myself here in Shetland , using the best sourced natural ingredients including our very own Goats Milk. We have an amazing selection of soaps , including our skincare range of fragrance free, as well as our very popular Hand and Body Butters, Handfelted Shetland Wool Soap and a wide selection of handmade Gifts . Pop in along and you might be lucky enough to meet our very own Little Miss Goatee. We pride ourselves by not using any parabens or SLS&rsquo;s, we also care about the conservation of our planet and therefore you wont find Palm Oil in any of our products. We are proud to be the first business in Scotland to have achieved Palm Oil Free Certification for all of our products.$q$ where id = 'fdda4cbe-1e28-4f4d-89d8-aed8317be513';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Lerwick Harbour, with modern, versatile facilities for a wide variety of users, is the principal commercial port for Shetland and a key component in the islands&rsquo; economy. At the crossroads of the North Sea and North-east Atlantic, Lerwick Harbour is Britain&rsquo;s &ldquo;Top Port&rdquo; &ndash; the most northerly commercial harbour in the country. With two entrances, the sheltered, deep-water port is open to shipping in all weathers and operates around the clock, handling over 5,000 vessels annually.$q$ where id = '810ae10f-4716-4076-be48-bf4cc6ba081e';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Jamieson&rsquo;s is a family owned business, which has specialised in wool from the native Shetland sheep for 5 generations. The family are dedicated to the survival of this unique fibre and as each new generation joins the business, this promotion becomes their life&rsquo;s ambition. The business was started in the early 1890&rsquo;s. Set up by Robert Jamieson in Sandness, on the far west coast of the Shetland Isles. From his shop, he bought or exchanged for goods, knitwear from the local crofters. The knitted goods were then sold on to meet the public demand for fashionable Shetland hosiery beyond the island&rsquo;s shores.$q$ where id = '83190905-d239-4a78-9cd4-ce565582bf56';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Jack Rae trained as a jeweller in Edinburgh and moved to the island of Foula in Shetland in 1945. He later moved to Weisdale on the Shetland mainland and started making Jewellery under the name of Shetland Silvercraft in 1953. After his son, Ken Rae, joined the business he bought over what was then &ldquo;The Gift Shop&rdquo; and started trading under the name of J G Rae Ltd in 1965. Ken Rae managed the business for more than 20 years, and had a break of about 8 years before returning in 2000. He now mainly looks after the manufacturing division &ndash; renamed Shetland Jewellery.$q$ where id = '134a0312-1442-453d-a760-3f591aa3370f';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Scotland&rsquo;s leading independent fuel distributor. We are committed to providing outstanding, professional customer service and we pride ourselves on our reliable and efficient deliveries to homes and businesses throughout Scotland. Since our business started in 1957 in Inverness, we have expanded and now operate from 12 depots across Scotland, servicing both the domestic and commercial markets. Contact our team on 0800 224 224 to receive free friendly advice and information on all of our products and services.$q$ where id = '3adff17b-05d7-4a7b-b7b6-496a565b7083';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$A warm welcome from Jigar and his friendly staff awaits at Coffee Culture, a delightful caf&eacute; in the heart of Lerwick. Known for its cozy atmosphere and exceptional service, Coffee Culture is the perfect spot to relax and enjoy a delicious snack. At Coffee Culture you can expect: Beverages: A variety of hot and cold drinks, including expertly brewed coffee, specialty teas, and refreshing juices. Sandwiches & Paninis: A delectable selection of freshly made sandwiches and paninis, prepared with high-quality ingredients. Salads: A diverse salad counter offering healthy and tasty options to suit every preference. Cakes & Desserts: An array of mouth-watering cakes and desserts, perfect for satisfying any sweet tooth. Jigar and his team provide a friendly and inviting environment where everyone feels at home. Download the HOPT app to order online. The HOPT App allows customers to order online and collect when they want.$q$ where id = '765b21ee-8fa2-46dd-bdbe-b10bcfc7c657';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Shetland Sports & Footwear is a premier retailer located in the heart of Lerwick, specialising in footwear, sports goods, and clothing. Serving the local community with a wide range of high-quality products. What Shoppers Will Find: &bull; Footwear: A vast selection of athletic shoes, casual footwear, and specialty sports shoes for all ages and activities. &bull; Sports Goods: Equipment and accessories for various sports, including football, running, swimming, and more. &bull; Clothing: Performance apparel, casual wear, and activewear for men, women, and children, suitable for both sports and everyday use. &bull; Accessories: Sports bags, socks, hats, and other essential accessories to complement any sporting activity. Opening hours: Monday to Saturday; 9:00am to 5:00pm$q$ where id = '7b4289b2-d565-4e0f-b941-904521cc94ad';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Welcome to C'est la Vie &ndash; A Taste of France in the Heart of Lerwick Nestled in the centre of Lerwick, Shetland, C'est la Vie is a French-inspired restaurant that offers an authentic taste of France in a cosy, welcoming setting. Whether for a casual meal or a quick bite, the restaurant&rsquo;s menu is designed to captivate diners with its delicious range of French classics. With a warm and inviting atmosphere, C'est la Vie prides itself on creating a relaxing dining experience. The staff are fluent in English, Spanish, and, of course, French, ensuring every guest feels at home. For those looking to experience a slice of French life in Lerwick, C'est la Vie offers a delightful culinary escape. Book a table today and savour life&rsquo;s simple pleasures &ndash; because after all, C'est la Vie!$q$ where id = '8894d173-a4c9-4f0f-a887-93ca9b7737cf';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Burns Lane Clothing &ndash; it&rsquo;s right up your street Opened in May 2018 Owners Ian Pagulayan and Michael Laurenson decided to expand from their already successful Sports/Outdoor business&rsquo; Cee & Jays and Intersport to fashion retail. Burns Lane Clothing is a new venture into ladies and mens designer clothing, footwear and accessories, providing Commercial Street with affordable current high street trends with a unique individual feel. Keen to work with brands such as Selected Femme/Homme that are committed to making their collections as sustainable as possible to help save our environment. Burns Lane Clothing also welcomes local designers from around Shetland to sell their products instore to support their creativity and businesses. Proud to stock &ndash; Drummie Bee, HM Textiles, Angela Irvine and Sew Knot Knitted.$q$ where id = 'e08070b8-dc56-47e2-93b6-c6aa66a5d21c';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$BML Accounts is run by Ben Laurenson, an experienced tax manager with over seventeen years of working in accountancy. A member of the Association of Accounting Technicians and the Association of Tax Technicians, Ben is skilled in tax preparation, private clients, accounting, partnership taxation, and tax accounting. He is also proficient with helping professionals working at sea, and is considered an expert nationally in the field of Seafarer&rsquo;s Earnings Discount (SED). Choosing BML means choosing a client focused service: Ben is committed to providing a service based on trust and transparency, and having worked as an accountant in Shetland for 17 years, is well placed to work closely with local companies.$q$ where id = '11da7f3c-aa82-4248-b3eb-7f63b88c9105';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Health and Beauty: Irene is HND trained with over 33 years experience as an Intense Pulsed Light (IPL) therapist, and also offers skin rejuvenation, electrolysis and advanced electrolysis. Book an appointment for a consultation or treatment on 01595 694496. Jade Keenan Aesthetics: Jade is a NVQ Level 2 and 3 trained beauty therapist offering a range of services from the salon: IPL, skin rejuvenation, carbon facials, electrolysis, LVL lash lift and waxing. Call for an appointment &ndash; 07722 182310 or email for more details: jadekeenanaethetics@gmail.com Services Offered: Hair Removal Lash and Brow Treatments Manicures, pedicures, and other nail services to keep your hands and feet looking their best.$q$ where id = 'df6ecd2f-b27a-40c5-91a0-41b5599c5019';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Boots is the UK&rsquo;s leading pharmacy-led health and beauty retailer. With around 2,500 stores ranging from local community pharmacies to large destination health and beauty stores, our purpose is to help our customers look and feel better than they ever thought possible. Boots UK is part of the Retail Pharmacy International Division of Walgreens Boots Alliance, Inc, the first global pharmacy-led health and wellbeing enterprise.$q$ where id = '4a865e42-9078-495d-9dbd-e938fa1a57f7';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Aura Lounge Ltd is a local beauty retreat offering a wide range of beauty treatments in a relaxing and welcoming environment. Whether you&rsquo;re looking to unwind or enjoy a little self-care, Aura Lounge provides professional treatments designed to help you look and feel your best.$q$ where id = '01869f1b-ff5f-40fc-9afe-07f3474b2b69';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Solicitors, Notary Public & Estate Agents Founded in 1882 by John Bannatyne Anderson, the firm added the name Goodlad when the present Partner&rsquo;s grandfather, the late Peter Goodlad, joined the Firm in the 1930s. As Shetland&rsquo;s longest established Firm, our office has always been located in the heart of Lerwick, first at 58 and now at 52 Commercial Street, Lerwick. Being in the centre of town, banks, building societies and other business organisations are easily accessible. We also provide a ramp for wheel chair and pram access. Legal services we provide to the community:- Adult With Incapacity Law, Crofting Law, Executries, Wills & Trusts, Family Law, Housing Landlord & Tenant, Residential Conveyancing and Estate Agency to name a few.$q$ where id = 'af3742f5-1f28-4c62-9d64-fd889cd0c8c0';
update public.local_businesses set description = $q$Anderson & Co is an old established family firm trading in Shetland knitwear, crafts, children&rsquo;s clothes and nursery products. Founded in 1873 by Thomas Anderson, Anderson's produce an extensive range of classically styled garments for adults and children in genuine Shetland wool renowned for its softness and warmth. They also stock a wide range of accessories including traditional Fair Isles, lightweight lace, seamless Shetland sweaters and chunky hand knitted ski sweaters. Also in stock are spinning wheels, patterns, wool and knitting books$q$ where id = 'bbb990ce-2bf1-4284-ac64-32191a750818';
